<rml>
<head>
	<title>vector stack</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="/folio/folio.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="/UI/vectors.rcss"/>
	<style>
		/*
			A multi-colour drawing rebuilt from stacked distance fields, sized by width alone.

			Every layer is absolutely positioned, so the container has no height of its own. The
			frame image is what supplies one: RCSS has no aspect-ratio, and an image element's
			intrinsic size is the only thing that carries a ratio. Without it the box collapses and
			the drawing does not render at all.

			wide.svg is 400x150, so the magenta container must be exactly covered by the drawing's
			own blue background at every size. Any magenta showing means the frame and the art
			disagree. Re-bake with:

			  msdfbake vector --in Tools/uipreview/tests/vectors/wide.svg
			                  --out Tools/uipreview/tests/UI/art
			                  --rcss Tools/uipreview/tests/UI/vectors.rcss --layers
		*/
		body
		{
			background-color: #202028;
			color: #ffffff;
			font-family: Inter;
			font-size: 13dp;
			padding: 16dp;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			box-sizing: border-box;
		}

		p { margin-bottom: 4dp; }

		/* Shows through anywhere the stack is the wrong shape. */
		.probe { background-color: #ff00ff; margin-bottom: 16dp; }

		.w400 { width: 400dp; }
		.w200 { width: 200dp; }
		.w96  { width: 96dp; }
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<p>400dp wide</p>
	<div class="wide-stack probe w400">
		<img class="wide-frame" sprite="wide_frame"/>
		<img class="wide_0-ink" sprite="wide_0"/>
		<img class="wide_1-ink" sprite="wide_1"/>
		<img class="wide_2-ink" sprite="wide_2"/>
	</div>

	<p>200dp wide</p>
	<div class="wide-stack probe w200">
		<img class="wide-frame" sprite="wide_frame"/>
		<img class="wide_0-ink" sprite="wide_0"/>
		<img class="wide_1-ink" sprite="wide_1"/>
		<img class="wide_2-ink" sprite="wide_2"/>
	</div>

	<p>96dp wide</p>
	<div class="wide-stack probe w96">
		<img class="wide-frame" sprite="wide_frame"/>
		<img class="wide_0-ink" sprite="wide_0"/>
		<img class="wide_1-ink" sprite="wide_1"/>
		<img class="wide_2-ink" sprite="wide_2"/>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
